####################################################################################################
# Y1 -- LOWER-semicontinuity atom extraction: Portmanteau direction, adversaries, topologies
####################################################################################################
  reference YM-like measure  nu = 0.30*delta_{1.0} + 0.70*delta_{3.0}
  edge atom at m=1.0, weight w=0.30

====================================================================================================
[P] PORTMANTEAU, FIXED POINT -- closed set {m}: limsup nu_n({m}) <= nu({m})  (UPPER, not lower)
====================================================================================================
  BUMP: nu_h = 0.30*Unif[1.0-h,1.0+h] + 0.70*delta_{3.0}   (atom at m spread to a density)
  test fns (continuous): phi1=exp(-s), phi2=s, phi3=cos(s), phi4=1/(1+s^2)
         h    I[phi1]    I[phi2]    I[phi3]    I[phi4]      nu_h({m})          nu({m})
       0.5   0.149871   2.400000  -0.537574   0.225744       0.000000         0.300000
       0.1   0.145399   2.400000  -0.531174   0.220249       0.000000         0.300000
      0.02   0.145222   2.400000  -0.530915   0.220010       0.000000         0.300000
     0.004   0.145215   2.400000  -0.530904   0.220000       0.000000         0.300000
     0.001   0.145215   2.400000  -0.530904   0.220000       0.000000         0.300000
  -> all weak-* integrals converge to nu's values (integrals match to ~1e-4..1e-6);
     BUT nu_h({m}) = 0 for every h>0 while nu({m}) = 0.30 : the fixed-point atom DISAPPEARS.
     liminf nu_h({m}) = 0 < 0.30 = nu({m}).  LSC FAILS in weak-*.  [T]
     (Portmanteau for the CLOSED set {m} gives only limsup<=nu({m}); it is USC, the WRONG side.)

====================================================================================================
[S] SPLIT ADVERSARY -- atom at m shatters symmetrically; converges in W_p, moments, every cont-at-m topology
====================================================================================================
  nu_h = 0.15*delta_{1.0-h} + 0.15*delta_{1.0+h} + 0.70*delta_{3.0}
         h        W_1        W_2        |dM1|        |dM2|        |dM3|        nu_h({m})
       0.3   0.090000   0.164317    0.000e+00    2.700e-02    8.100e-02         0.000000
       0.1   0.030000   0.054772    0.000e+00    3.000e-03    9.000e-03         0.000000
      0.02   0.006000   0.010954    0.000e+00    1.200e-04    3.600e-04         0.000000
     0.004   0.001200   0.002191    0.000e+00    4.800e-06    1.440e-05         0.000000
     0.001   0.000300   0.000548    0.000e+00    3.000e-07    9.000e-07         0.000000
  -> W_1, W_2 -> 0 and all moments match, yet nu_h({m}) = 0 < 0.30 = nu({m}).
     Any topology generated by functions CONTINUOUS AT m (W_p all p, moments, vague,
     SOT/WOT states on C(K), L^inf-normal states) contains this sequence -> LSC FAILS.  [T]/[NG]

====================================================================================================
[T] TV / C*-NORM -- fixed-point atom continuous, but only by the TRIVIAL bound (circular)
====================================================================================================
  bump family, TV distance to nu:
     h=     0.5   ||bump - nu||_TV = 0.600000   (nu_bump({m})=0.000, nu({m})=0.300)
     h=     0.1   ||bump - nu||_TV = 0.600000   (nu_bump({m})=0.000, nu({m})=0.300)
     h=    0.02   ||bump - nu||_TV = 0.600000   (nu_bump({m})=0.000, nu({m})=0.300)
     h=   0.004   ||bump - nu||_TV = 0.600000   (nu_bump({m})=0.000, nu({m})=0.300)
  -> ||bump - nu||_TV = 2w = 0.60 CONSTANT (never ->0): the bump is NOT TV-convergent.
     TV controls the atom by the exact bound |nu({m})-nu'({m})| <= ||nu-nu'||_TV.
     But that bound IS the definition: {m} is a Borel set, so 1_{m} is in the TV test class;
     'nu({m}) is TV-continuous' <=> 'nu({m}) is a BOUNDED functional on M(K)' <=> |nu({m})|<=||nu||.
     Zero content / CIRCULAR: the topology already contains the atom indicator.  [T]/(circular)

====================================================================================================
[E] EDGE ATOM  E(nu)=nu({inf supp nu})  IS DISCONTINUOUS EVEN IN TV  (the location jumps)
====================================================================================================
  nu_e = (e/2)*delta_e + (1-e/2)*delta_2 ;  inf supp nu_e = e ;  E(nu_e) = e/2
           e ||nu_e-d2||_TV  inf supp nu_e  E(nu_e)=nu_e({e})       E(delta_2) LSC? (E_lim<=liminf)
         0.5   5.000000e-01            0.5           0.250000         1.000000               NO
         0.2   2.000000e-01            0.2           0.100000         1.000000               NO
        0.05   5.000000e-02           0.05           0.025000         1.000000               NO
        0.01   1.000000e-02           0.01           0.005000         1.000000               NO
       0.001   1.000000e-03          0.001           0.000500         1.000000               NO
  -> nu_e -> delta_2 in TV (||nu_e-delta_2||_TV = e -> 0), yet
     E(nu_e) = e/2 -> 0  while  E(delta_2) = 1 :  liminf E = 0 < 1 = E(lim).  LSC FAILS in TV.
     CAUSE: inf supp (the LOCATION) jumps e -> 2 along a TV-convergent sequence.  Location is
     discontinuous in every topology coarser than TV; controlling it = resolving the gap. [T]/[NG]

====================================================================================================
[C] THIN ATOM -- chi=1/L for ALL e, but edge atom w=e/2L -> 0  (continuity gives NO uniform floor)
====================================================================================================
  nu_e=w delta_e+(1-w)delta_{s2},  w=e/(2L),  s2=2L(1-w)  (the corpus thin atom)
           e         w=e/2L   chi=int s^-1 dnu      edge atom w       edge m=e
         0.5       0.250000           1.000000         0.250000            0.5
         0.2       0.100000           1.000000         0.100000            0.2
        0.05       0.025000           1.000000         0.025000           0.05
        0.01       0.005000           1.000000         0.005000           0.01
       0.001       0.000500           1.000000         0.000500          0.001
  -> chi=1/L EXACTLY for every e; edge atom w=e/2L -> 0.  Continuity/LSC of the atom reads the
     TRUE (small) value; it can NEVER certify f1^2 >= r0 uniformly.  Thin atom NOT certified. [T]

====================================================================================================
[A] FREE-FIELD ACID TEST -- finite-L free field is finitely ATOMIC (f1^2>0); acid is L->inf
====================================================================================================
  continuum free massless cut proxy rho(s)=const on [0,1]: atomless, f1^2=0  (R3 [S2]).
  BUT at finite L a free field on T^4_L has DISCRETE spectrum -> its KL measure has atoms;
     lowest mode ~ (2pi/L)^2, with a positive edge weight f1^2>0 at finite L.
  => any topology that yields LSC/continuity of the atom also gives a POSITIVE atom on the
     finite-L free field.  It does NOT discriminate free vs YM at finite L; the acid test is
     an L->inf statement -- exactly where no TV/strong convergence is available.  [T]/[NG]

====================================================================================================
[OPS] OPERATOR-ALGEBRAIC / C*-SEMINORM TOPOLOGIES -- all collapse
====================================================================================================
  (a) states on commutative C*-algebra C(K); SOT/WOT/weak-* = sigma(C*,C): atom USC only. FAIL LSC.
  (b) states on von Neumann algebra L^inf(K); weak-* = sigma(A*,A) same as (a); the ATOM is a
      SINGULAR (non-normal) state -- normal-state convergence (=TV on a.c. part) does not see it. FAIL.
  (c) pure states / spectral projectors carry atom PRESENCE (a rank), NOT the weight: the
      decomposition nu = w delta_m + (1-w) nu_c reads w as the coefficient of an EXTREME point;
      that coefficient map is weak-* discontinuous (pure states are not weakly closed). FAIL for weight.
  (d) any C*-norm/seminorm controlling point masses = TV: gives continuity only circularly (cf [T]).
  => no operator-algebraic topology gives NON-CIRCULAR LSC of the atom WEIGHT.  [NG]

====================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  [P]  weak-* gives USC (limsup<=), LSC FALSE; bump makes the fixed-point atom disappear.  [T]
  [S]  split adversary converges in W_p / moments / every cont-at-m topology; LSC FALSE there. [T]/[NG]
  [T]  TV/C*-norm makes the FIXED-POINT atom continuous, but trivially (|nu({m})|<=||nu||_TV):
       CIRCULAR, and unattainable (bump is TV-far, ||.||_TV=2w const).                        [T]/circular
  [E]  the EDGE atom E(nu)=nu({inf supp nu}) is discontinuous EVEN IN TV (location jump e->2).  [T]
  [C]  thin atom: continuity/LSC reads the true small atom, gives NO uniform floor r0.         [T]
  [A]  finite-L free field is atomic; topology LSC does not discriminate free vs YM.           [T]/[NG]
  KILL: LSC is FALSE in every non-circular topology (split/bump adversary), and the physical
  EDGE atom is discontinuous even in TV (location).  LSC is TRUE only in norm/TV-type topologies
  that are (i) CIRCULAR (atom = bounded functional, tautology) and (ii) UNATTAINABLE from finite
  (L,a)-data -- and even there only for the fixed-point weight, NOT the edge atom.  PROPOSAL DEAD. [NG]
  Clay 0%.  No QED.
